# Cursor Rules for BLE LED Control Device

## Project Overview
This is a BLE LED control device project using STM32WB55 microcontroller and Flutter mobile application.

## Code Style and Standards

### C/C++ (STM32)
- Use snake_case for functions and variables
- Use UPPER_SNAKE_CASE for constants and macros
- Use PascalCase for structs and enums
- File naming: module__function.c (e.g., ble__service.c)
- Maximum 500 lines per file
- Maximum 50 lines per function
- Always include header guards in .h files
- Use meaningful variable names
- Add comments for complex logic

### Dart/Flutter
- Use camelCase for variables and functions
- Use PascalCase for classes and enums
- Use snake_case for file names
- Follow Flutter style guide
- Use const constructors where possible
- Prefer composition over inheritance

### Documentation
- All public functions must have documentation
- Use Doxygen-style comments for C/C++
- Use Dart documentation comments for Flutter
- Update docs/Project.md when architecture changes
- Update docs/Tasktracker.md when tasks are completed
- Add entries to docs/Diary.md for technical decisions

## Project Structure

### STM32 (Embedded)
```
App/           # Application layer
Core/          # System files (main, tasks, FreeRTOS)
Drivers/       # Hardware drivers (HAL, custom)
Services/      # High-level services (BLE, LED control)
Utils/         # Utility functions
Test/          # Test files
docs/          # Project documentation
```

### Flutter (Mobile)
```
lib/
├── main.dart
├── models/     # Data models
├── services/   # BLE service, business logic
├── widgets/    # UI components
├── screens/    # App screens
└── utils/      # Utility functions
```

## Development Workflow

### Before Starting Work
1. Check docs/Tasktracker.md for current tasks
2. Read docs/Diary.md for recent decisions
3. Review docs/qa.md for unanswered questions
4. Update task status when starting work

### During Development
1. Follow the established code style
2. Add appropriate error handling
3. Test functionality thoroughly
4. Update documentation as needed
5. Add entries to docs/Diary.md for important decisions

### After Completing Work
1. Update docs/Tasktracker.md with progress
2. Add entry to docs/Diary.md if needed
3. Update docs/Project.md if architecture changed
4. Test the complete system
5. Commit with descriptive messages

## BLE Protocol Standards

### Service UUID
- LED Control Service: `12345678-1234-1234-1234-123456789ABC`

### Characteristics
- LED State: `87654321-4321-4321-4321-CBA987654321`
- LED Individual: `11111111-2222-3333-4444-555555555555`
- System Status: `AAAAAAAA-BBBB-CCCC-DDDD-EEEEEEEEEEEE`

### Data Formats
- LED State: 1 byte (bit mask for 4 LEDs)
- LED Individual: 2 bytes (ID + state)
- System Status: 4 bytes (status, errors, temperature)

## Testing Requirements

### STM32 Testing
- Unit tests for all services
- Integration tests for BLE functionality
- Hardware tests for LED control
- Performance tests for response time

### Flutter Testing
- Unit tests for business logic
- Widget tests for UI components
- Integration tests for BLE communication
- E2E tests for complete workflow

## Security Guidelines

### BLE Security
- Use Just Works security for MVP
- Implement MAC address filtering
- Validate all incoming commands
- Log security events

### Code Security
- Validate all input parameters
- Check buffer boundaries
- Use secure random number generation
- Implement proper error handling

## Performance Requirements

### Response Time
- BLE command to LED change: < 100ms
- BLE scanning: < 5 seconds
- Reconnection: < 3 seconds

### Power Consumption
- Standby mode: < 1mA
- Active mode: < 10mA
- BLE transmission: < 20mA

## Error Handling

### STM32 Error Handling
- Use error codes for all functions
- Implement error logging system
- Add watchdog timer
- Graceful degradation on errors

### Flutter Error Handling
- Use try-catch blocks appropriately
- Show user-friendly error messages
- Log errors for debugging
- Implement retry mechanisms

## Version Control

### Commit Messages
- Use conventional commit format
- Include task number if applicable
- Describe what and why, not how
- Keep commits atomic and focused

### Branch Strategy
- main: production-ready code
- develop: integration branch
- feature/*: new features
- bugfix/*: bug fixes
- release/*: release preparation

## Documentation Updates

### When to Update Project.md
- Architecture changes
- New requirements
- Technology stack changes
- Performance requirements updates

### When to Update Tasktracker.md
- Task completion
- New tasks added
- Priority changes
- Timeline adjustments

### When to Update Diary.md
- Technical decisions made
- Problems encountered and solved
- Important observations
- Next steps planned

## Code Review Checklist

### STM32 Code Review
- [ ] Follows naming conventions
- [ ] Proper error handling
- [ ] Memory management
- [ ] BLE protocol compliance
- [ ] Performance considerations
- [ ] Documentation updated

### Flutter Code Review
- [ ] Follows Flutter style guide
- [ ] Proper state management
- [ ] BLE communication working
- [ ] UI/UX considerations
- [ ] Error handling
- [ ] Testing coverage

## Emergency Procedures

### Build Failures
1. Check Makefile for syntax errors
2. Verify all source files exist
3. Check include paths
4. Review recent changes

### BLE Issues
1. Check device compatibility
2. Verify UUIDs match
3. Test with BLE scanner
4. Review protocol implementation

### Flutter Issues
1. Check BLE permissions
2. Verify device compatibility
3. Test on both platforms
4. Review BLE library version

